<ui:UXML xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:ui="UnityEngine.UIElements" xmlns:uie="UnityEditor.UIElements" noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../../UIElementsSchema/UIElements.xsd" editor-extension-mode="False">
    <ui:VisualElement name="Screen" style="flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 0; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <ui:ScrollView horizontal-scroller-visibility="Hidden" style="flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 28px; padding-top: -46px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
            <ui:Label text="Welcome Commander!&#10;&#10;**********************&#10;&#10;The Galaxy needs you to save it!&#10;Sadly, the only men we had on hand are fresh out of training, they&apos;ll need to learn on the fly through your commands!&#10;&#10;There are 4 dimensions to commanding your troops:&#10;- 1: &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;RECON&lt;/color&gt; vs &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;ENGAGE&lt;/color&gt;; Recon tells them to focus on discovering the enemy ship, engage tells them to worry about attacking enemy ships.&#10;&#10;- 2: &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;DEFENSE&lt;/color&gt; vs &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;ASSAULT&lt;/color&gt;; tells them to focus more on either defending our mothership, or trying to destroy the enemy&apos;s mothership instead.&#10;&#10;-3: &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;TACTICS&lt;/color&gt; vs &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;STRATEGY&lt;/color&gt;; this one tells the troops to other look at the long game, and consider all the combat they&apos;ve seen up to that point, or, focus on adapting immediately to the enemies tactics. This one might take some getting used to.&#10;&#10;- 4: &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;DOCTRINE&lt;/color&gt; vs &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;CHANGE&lt;/color&gt;: This is for telling the troops how much they need to either focus on staying alive, or trying to follow your orders. I know it&apos;s weird to tell your soldiers to ignore your orders, but we can&apos;t win a war with a bunch of dead men.&#10;&#10;You can customize your command doctrine or choose from one of 4 &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;PRESET&lt;/color&gt; options. Try to find the one that is the most effective!&#10;&#10;**********************&#10;&#10;Speaking of which, try to keep your pilots alive commander. They may be dumber than a box of rocks at the start, but these boys learn quick. The longer they fight, the smarter they get!&#10;&#10;For now we only can supply you with 2 types of ships, &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;FIGHTERS&lt;/color&gt; and &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;RESUPPLY&lt;/color&gt;. You already know what the fighters do, but the resupply ships keep your fighters going. Without them, that little yellow bar beneath the fighter&apos;s health will go empty, leaving that ship stranded in the middle of space. I shouldn&apos;t have to tell you why that&apos;s bad.&#10;&#10;You can give your ships target priorities by using the &lt;color=#00FF00&gt;PRIORITY&lt;/color&gt; command.&#10;&#10;Keep your eye on the enemy and your own ships commander, it may look like your troops aren&apos;t obeying your orders, but they&apos;re just trying to figure it out, give them a bit of time. Well, that should be just about everything.&#10;&#10;Oh, and one more thing before we let you go, if you are under direct attack at your mothership, use the DEFEND action to fire onenemy ships.&#10;&#10;**********************&#10;&#10;Good luck out there commander, and God&apos;s speed!&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;" name="IntroText" style="position: absolute; -unity-font-definition: url(&quot;project://database/Assets/UI/Fonts/Orbitron-VariableFont_wght.ttf?fileID=12800000&amp;guid=eb064b633966b4a1ba60e1eaa101014a&amp;type=3#Orbitron-VariableFont_wght&quot;); color: rgb(232, 209, 203); font-size: 44px; padding-bottom: 2%; top: 0%; -unity-text-outline-width: 2px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(255, 54, 0); flex-grow: 1; padding-top: 99px; flex-wrap: wrap; white-space: normal; max-width: 100%;"/>
            <ui:Button text="BEGIN!" name="StartGame" style="position: absolute; align-content: center; justify-content: flex-end; align-self: flex-start; top: 90%; -unity-font-definition: url(&quot;project://database/Assets/UI/Fonts/Orbitron-VariableFont_wght.ttf?fileID=12800000&amp;guid=eb064b633966b4a1ba60e1eaa101014a&amp;type=3#Orbitron-VariableFont_wght&quot;); color: rgb(226, 199, 199); background-color: rgb(166, 21, 62); width: 20%; padding-top: 8px;"/>
        </ui:ScrollView>
    </ui:VisualElement>
</ui:UXML>
